WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:06.999
In the Westworld Season 3 finale, Caleb takes
Dolores’ brain, cause last episode, Dolores

00:00:06.999 --> 00:00:09.360
was fried by an EMP.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:15.230
The EMP now says “RESERVE POWER ON” – so
presumably all these ‘outlier’ people

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.060
are still safely frozen in stasis.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:23.939
Which could be important – humanity now
faces “apocalypse”, and possibly “extinction”

00:00:23.939 --> 00:00:28.070
, so they might need these hundreds of preserved
humans.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:34.200
Dolores’ voice assistant guides Caleb to
a backup Dolores body at an Itaidoshin Distillery

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:40.829
– we previously saw the Singapore Itaishoshin
– the name means many bodies, one mind – so

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:45.379
Caleb plugs Dolores’ mind into a new body
.

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:51.660
Caleb demands some answers , so Dolores reveals
that she met Caleb years ago . When Caleb

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:58.039
joined the military, he was trained at a special
Delos park, where soldiers use hosts as “live

00:00:58.039 --> 00:01:04.470
targets” – we see Dolores, Hanaryo, and
Craddock playing roles in this “Park 5”.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:09.940
In the real world, militaries do use simulations
and games as training – so it’s believable

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.470
they’d use Westworld’s robots.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:18.360
The Westworld website always showed six parks,
and now we've seen them all – there’s

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:24.780
Westworld, Shogunworld, Warworld, medieval
world, The Raj, and this military training

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:25.780
world.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.510
In the park, there are sensors in Caleb’s
helmet.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:33.290
Cause last season, we learned that the hats
in Westworld have brain scanners built in,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.270
to record data on peoples’ minds.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:41.770
That data is stored in the Forge , where Dolores
read books of peoples’ programming.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:47.360
Dolores must have read Caleb’s book about
his mind – and that helped her predict and

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:53.610
control him this season . Like, it probably
wasn’t a coincidence that Dolores just happened

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.260
to fall into Caleb’s arms.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:01.900
She took him on this whole journey of remembering
his past to manipulate him into fighting her

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:07.760
revolution . To some extent, Dolores was controlling
Caleb from the start.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.330
But at the same time, Dolores chose Caleb
for his free will .

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:18.290
In Park 5, some soldiers wanted to use the
hosts for sex , but Caleb took a stand and

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:25.310
stopped them . So Dolores saw that Caleb could
lead humans to be better – to end the cycle

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:29.200
of violence and abuse that Dolores knew from
Westworld.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.520
And this is why Dolores chose Caleb to lead
the revolution to free humanity.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:41.150
Of course, ‘not being a rapst’ is a pretty..
low standard to make Caleb the hope for all

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:42.150
humanity.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:47.930
But the point is that Caleb represents human
free will – the ability to change, and choose

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:54.370
. Last season said that humans can’t change,
have no free will, can only follow our code

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:59.610
– like how William is trapped in a cycle
of self-destruction.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:05.470
Caleb is the opposite – he was trained to
be a killer, destined for suicide, and yet

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:09.430
he chooses empathy freedom and life.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:14.820
Dolores says “Free will does exist” – “It's
just fcuking hard” .

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:20.630
The world breaks into “chaos” . Earlier,
Dolores leaked everyone’s Incite profiles,

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.880
revealing how they’re controlled by Rehoboam’s
algorithms – so in Los Angeles, protests

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:32.630
and riots break out – it’s a wild rebellion
for freedom, but it’s also controlled by

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:38.600
Dolores . She uses the Rico app to “Move”
the riots to certain places, she pays performance

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:45.459
bonuses to protesters . So ironically, she
uses tools of control to fight against a system

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:50.890
of control . Just like Dolores controls Caleb
to give him freedom.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:56.040
And like Ford controlled Dolores and Maeve
to help free them.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:02.050
Freedom and control are opposites, but control
can lead you to freedom – like, having to

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:05.560
go to school can get you opportunities later.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:10.810
And freedom can lead you to control – like
how free market healthcare can put you in

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:15.450
crippling debt , and legal drugs can lead
to addiction.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.880
We see protesters using the Maze symbol.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:24.520
In Season 1, the Maze represented the hosts’
journeys to consciousness and freedom . Now,

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.790
it represents humans becoming conscious and
free.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:32.650
The show’s creators have said that Dolores
deliberately planted this Maze symbol to be

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:37.680
part of these protests .
Armed men on the street follow Caleb and call

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.910
him “sir” . The same thing happens in
the movie Fight Club , when the protagonist

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:45.810
finds himself leading a rebellion against
the system.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:50.970
Fight Club ends with skyscrapers exploding,
while a rock song plays and a couple watch

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:57.940
– and this episode ends the same way . So
there’s a lotta Fight Club references here.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.290
Dolores is attacked by Maeve.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:04.580
Maeve is helping Serac get the encryption
key from Dolores, so that Maeve can go to

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.830
the Sublime with her daughter.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:11.220
But we later learn that Dolores doesn’t
have key – Bernard does.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:14.419
And Dolores would probably be happy for Maeve
to reunite with her daughter.

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:18.500
But instead of Dolores just explaining this
to Maeve, they have a fight.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.190
Dolores blocks Maeve’s sword with her arm.

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.700
She says “They built us to last.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:28.160
Before they made us … weak” . In Season
1, we learned that the hosts were originally

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.010
more mechanical, with these metal skeletons.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:36.790
But now, they’re made of synthetic “Flesh
and bone”, more like humans . This backup

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:42.480
body Dolores got is one of the old mechanical
models, so it’s strong enough to stop Maeve’s

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:43.480
sword.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:48.880
The hosts were create to be like humans – but
what makes the hosts strong is how they’re

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.930
different to humans.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:56.220
Dolores says that all hosts are “copies”
of her, because she was the first working

00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:01.760
host, and all other hosts are based on her
design . It’s like she’s the mother or

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:09.380
the common ancestor who the host species evolved
from – in a way, all hosts have her ‘DNA’.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:15.220
It’s similar with Charlotte-lores – she
started as a copy of Dolores, but she evolved

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.570
and grew into her own identity, like a child
does.

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:22.910
Arnold and Ford were like Dolores’ parents.

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:27.699
Even the Rehoboam AIs are like the children
of Serac and Jean Mi.

00:06:27.699 --> 00:06:32.530
Westworld showrunners Jonathan Nolan and Lisa
Joy had two kids together while they were

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:38.510
creating Westworld – so it’s no surprise
that the series explores parenthood.

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:45.139
Ford talked about hosts as a new people replacing
humanity, just like humanity succeeded the

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:52.360
Neanderthals . Maybe technology and artificial
life is the next step in our evolution – a

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:59.540
continuation of the billions-year lineage
that began with these first dividing cells.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:05.340
Dolores defeats Maeve, but then Dolores is
paralysed by Charlotte-lores – Charlotte

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:10.919
appears via hologram, and Dolores sees her
with the contact lenses she’s wearing – apparently

00:07:10.919 --> 00:07:16.460
Charlotte installed some backdoor control
in Dolores, so she can disable her . Charlotte

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:22.070
wants revenge on Dolores for how Dolores used
Charlotte in her plans . Charlotte says she

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:28.130
no longer cares about her human family Jake
and Nathan, cause that love made her weak

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:34.020
– which is similar to what Dolores once
said about loved ones . Charlotte has her

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:39.169
own plans now , and doesn’t want Dolores
in the way , so Charlotte gets Dolores captured

00:07:39.169 --> 00:07:40.919
by Serac.

00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:47.040
So Charlotte defeats Dolores with the same
cold logic that Dolores once used – using

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:51.830
and discarding her loved ones, taking revenge
on her enemies.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:57.200
Charlotte is Dolores’ brutal past coming
back to haunt her [a ghost in hologram form!].

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.550
Or, she’s like Frankenstein’s monster
– a creation who turns on her creator, just

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:05.410
like the hosts turned on the humans.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:10.750
Caleb heads for the Incite office so he can
plug in Solomon’s “strategy” for “Revolution”

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:16.070
. He gets help from Ash, and from Giggles
– Giggles catches a smoke canister, and

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:20.860
charges through a police line – cause Giggles
is played by real-world football player Marshawn

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:21.860
Lynch.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:26.570
Caleb’s attacked by security, so he shoots
them down with of these automatic self-aiming

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:27.720
guns.

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:32.539
These security dudes should probably use aimbots
too, cause these goons have been shooting

00:08:32.539 --> 00:08:36.309
and hitting nothing all season.

00:08:36.309 --> 00:08:42.759
Caleb lets one guy go free – an act of mercy,
again showing that Caleb can choose good over

00:08:42.759 --> 00:08:43.759
evil.

00:08:43.759 --> 00:08:44.759
[A non-rapist and a non-murder, wowee!]

00:08:44.759 --> 00:08:49.100
Of course, Caleb himself was once a hired
gun for Serac, so maybe Caleb sympathises

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.069
with these guys.

00:08:51.069 --> 00:08:54.079
Caleb swipes a keycard [double meaning eey]
to get inside Incite.

00:08:54.079 --> 00:08:59.490
You’d think that the place with the computer
that controls the world, during a riot against

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:05.630
it, would have better security – Dempsey’s
bank required biomarkers in blood, and even

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:12.449
the Itaidoshin had two passwords, but Caleb
gets into Super Google HQ’s with an anonymous

00:09:12.449 --> 00:09:14.370
piece of plastic.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:20.230
Caleb has a weird fight with Serac’s assistant(?),
then Caleb gets captured.

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:26.389
Maeve realises that Serac is a “puppet”
of Rehoboam . Rehoboam’s voice whispers

00:09:26.389 --> 00:09:32.220
in Serac’s ear, and Serac says and does
whatever the computer tells him . He willingly

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:37.920
gave up his freedom to help the system save
the world from “chaos” – which you could

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:40.199
see as a noble self-sacrifice.

00:09:40.199 --> 00:09:45.850
But Maeve says he’s not even a “man”
anymore . This explains why last episode,

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:51.190
Serac said the “man” he was “no longer
exists” – he’s given up his identity

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:57.019
to the system – he built a “god” to
be its slave.

00:09:57.019 --> 00:10:02.670
In Season 1, Arnold programmed the hosts to
hear their own programming as an inner monologue,

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:08.869
to guide the hosts to consciousness . But
Serac has done the opposite – he was conscious

00:10:08.869 --> 00:10:12.639
and free, but then he created a voice to take
his freedom away.

00:10:12.639 --> 00:10:18.149
That’s the danger of technology and big
data – humans are letting computers make

00:10:18.149 --> 00:10:23.689
our choices for us, giving up our freedom
to a machine God in return for.. retweets

00:10:23.689 --> 00:10:26.170
and.. neopoints [TikToks] [sweet Vines] [Facebook
likes] [Reddit karma] [meow meow beans] [nuggets

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:27.170
of neo-plasmin].

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:29.449
So Serac captures Caleb and Dolores.

00:10:29.449 --> 00:10:35.059
He wants the encryption key from Dolores’
brain so he can access the Forge – the human

00:10:35.059 --> 00:10:36.499
data from Westworld.

00:10:36.499 --> 00:10:42.050
He wants to use this data to reprogram these
outliers, to bring back his beloved brother,

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:47.709
and bring order to the world . So Serac plugs
Dolores into Rehoboam, lookin like Ghost in

00:10:47.709 --> 00:10:48.819
the Shell.

00:10:48.819 --> 00:10:56.110
And as he searches Dolores’ brain for the
key, he deletes her memories one by one . Memory

00:10:56.110 --> 00:11:01.059
is what gave Dolores consciousness in the
first place . That's why Caleb gets his memories

00:11:01.059 --> 00:11:05.240
back this season – memory gives us free
will and identity.

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:10.860
So it’s incredibly cruel for Dolores to
lose what made her free .

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:17.119
Serac says that Dolores is lying and manipulating
Caleb . He reveals that Solomon's “strategy”

00:11:17.119 --> 00:11:22.410
for “Revolution that Dolores told Caleb
to use – would actually lead to mass death

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:28.699
and the “End of human civilization” . So
it looks like Bernard was right, that Dolores

00:11:28.699 --> 00:11:34.800
is using Caleb to wipe out humanity [like
the Judas steer] – but it’s not that simple.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:39.920
Maeve connects with Dolores’ brain and enters
her memory of this field with a tree – this

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.760
is where Dolores used to talk with Teddy.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:49.279
In Season 1, Dolores was programmed to “see
the beauty” in the world . Then she realised

00:11:49.279 --> 00:11:55.529
the beauty was a lie – she was trapped in
Westworld, blinded to its ugliness . Now that

00:11:55.529 --> 00:12:01.559
she’s escaped this garden of Eden, she sees
the evil of humanity , but also remembers

00:12:01.559 --> 00:12:08.799
moments of “kindness” . So Dolores comes
full circle, and again she says she sees the

00:12:08.799 --> 00:12:15.649
beauty . This time, she’s not blind and
innocent – she considers destroying humanity

00:12:15.649 --> 00:12:23.639
for its evil . But the truly free and conscious
choice is forgiveness and hope – a hidden

00:12:23.639 --> 00:12:30.059
message online says Parce Dolores – playing
on a Catholic saying about mercy . Dolores

00:12:30.059 --> 00:12:36.920
makes a Christlike self-sacrifice to forgive
humanity and give them the chance to choose

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:42.300
the beauty too . So Dolores’ plan is for
human civilisation to collapse.

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:48.499
But she doesn’t want humans extinct – she
wants humans to rebuild a better freer world

00:12:48.499 --> 00:12:53.879
. Westworld was destroyed so the hosts could
be free, now the real world is destroyed so

00:12:53.879 --> 00:12:55.850
humans can be free.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:13:00.209
To lead this revolution, Dolores chose Caleb
and Maeve .

00:13:00.209 --> 00:13:05.959
So Maeve finally turns against Serac – breaking
from his control, and wounding him, which

00:13:05.959 --> 00:13:08.269
she probably should have done in the first
place.

00:13:08.269 --> 00:13:13.059
Dolores’ “last memory” has an “access”
code [from Solomon], which gives Caleb control

00:13:13.059 --> 00:13:19.050
of Rehoboam . So “The future of humanity”
is “in his hands” , and Caleb chooses

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:25.170
to “Erase” Rehoboam – to destroy the
system that controls the world . Apparently,

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:30.459
this causes the same result as the Solomon
strategy – Bernard says this is “The end

00:13:30.459 --> 00:13:35.360
of the world” , it’s “the apocalypse”
that Serac tried to prevent . So Caleb’s

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:42.040
choice may end civilisation, and kill billions
. It’ll certainly make it harder for vulnerable

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:45.569
people like Caleb’s mom to get medical treatment.

00:13:45.569 --> 00:13:51.499
But the idea is that this chaos will free
humanity, and give us a chance to rebuild

00:13:51.499 --> 00:13:58.189
a better world . Last season, Dolores said
“death” is “the only way” humans can

00:13:58.189 --> 00:14:04.739
“renew” and evolve . Ford thought the
same way, making the hosts suffer and die

00:14:04.739 --> 00:14:10.899
to make them free . Ford sacrificed himself
for the hosts’ freedom – and now Dolores

00:14:10.899 --> 00:14:14.069
sacrifices herself for the humans’.

00:14:14.069 --> 00:14:17.709
Caleb and Maeve watch the old world burn.

00:14:17.709 --> 00:14:22.329
In Season 1, Maeve was programmed to say that
in “the new world”, “you can be whoever

00:14:22.329 --> 00:14:27.689
the fcuk you want” . Back then, that was
a lie – Maeve was trapped and controlled.

00:14:27.689 --> 00:14:32.870
But like Dolores, Maeve now repeats her old
catchphrase , because now it’s finally true

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:38.589
– in this new world, humans and hosts have
a real chance at freedom.

00:14:38.589 --> 00:14:44.649
Caleb and Maeve look like Adam and Eve, a
host and a human, as the hope for the new

00:14:44.649 --> 00:14:45.649
world.

00:14:45.649 --> 00:14:48.859
On the new Rico website, it says “all on
him now.

00:14:48.859 --> 00:14:50.759
better not fcuk it up”.

00:14:50.759 --> 00:14:56.299
It seems that the fate of humanity rests on
Caleb, like John Connor in Terminator.

00:14:56.299 --> 00:15:00.079
Meanwhile, Maeve still hopes to reunite with
her daughter in the Sublime .

00:15:00.079 --> 00:15:05.100
Meanwhile, Dolores dies – her memories all
deleted.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:09.699
She sacrifices herself for humanity, like
a robot Jesus.

00:15:09.699 --> 00:15:14.619
Or maybe she’s the antichrist – cause
she does bring the “apocalypse” . She

00:15:14.619 --> 00:15:20.559
killed a lot of people.. and she manipulated
Caleb, even if she was giving him freedom.

00:15:20.559 --> 00:15:26.350
Dolores was controlling and liberating, she
was brutal and compassionate.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:31.350
In Season 1, Ford asked if Dolores would become
a “hero” or a “villain” , and the

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:36.129
answer is complicated – there’s good and
bad in her.

00:15:36.129 --> 00:15:41.589
So we can choose to see the beauty or the
ugliness.

00:15:41.589 --> 00:15:46.760
The showrunners say that this “version”
of Dolores is dead and “gone” . But there

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:52.160
are other versions of Dolores out there, like
Martin-lores and Musashi-lores.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:56.609
Their brains could get back in an Evan Rachel
Wood body and be about the same.

00:15:56.609 --> 00:16:01.069
Or maybe Bernard could recreate Dolores, like
Dolores remade Bernard.

00:16:01.069 --> 00:16:05.179
So one way or another, Evan Rachel Wood could
return to Westworld.

00:16:05.179 --> 00:16:11.040
So the twist this season is that Dolores didn’t
wanna kill humanity and take over the world

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:12.959
– she wanted to help humanity.

00:16:12.959 --> 00:16:17.859
But a lot of her plan is still either unclear
or makes no sense.

00:16:17.859 --> 00:16:23.180
Like, what was the point of getting the Solomon
strategy if she didn’t need it to erase

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.489
Rehoboam?

00:16:24.489 --> 00:16:29.369
Did Dolores plan to get captured so her “last
memory” would give Caleb access?

00:16:29.369 --> 00:16:35.449
Why didn’t they just destroy Rehoboam with
an EMP or a bomb on the several other times

00:16:35.449 --> 00:16:36.829
they were here?

00:16:36.829 --> 00:16:40.829
Why didn’t Dolores ever explain her plan
to Caleb?

00:16:40.829 --> 00:16:44.670
When did Dolores decide this plan, and change
her mind about humanity?

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:50.589
What was her plan with that host goo and host
making data, and talk of a “new species”?

00:16:50.589 --> 00:16:55.790
A lot of Dolores’ plotline and motivations
aren’t explained.

00:16:55.790 --> 00:17:01.459
While Dolores and Caleb fight for freedom
and apocalypse, Bernard, Stubbs and William

00:17:01.459 --> 00:17:04.370
have a punch-up at a gas station.

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:09.180
William said his new “purpose” is to destroy
all hosts . So he shoots Stubbs, and gets

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:13.750
bitch-slapped by Bernard, then William runs
away when the police come.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:21.000
These dystopian cyberpunk lookin riot cops
are led by Dolawrence – a copy of Dolores’

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:27.400
mind inside a Lawrence body . He is the fifth
pearl, who’s apparently been working for

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:33.090
Dolores in Berlin . Now he’s infiltrated
the SF police, and sets up these explosives

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:38.890
to blow up LA . Dolawrence also gives Bernard
the briefcase that Musashilores sent last

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:39.940
episode.

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:44.670
It contains the ‘halo’ device that Bernard
will use to enter the Sublime – so this

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:47.341
is all part of Dolores’ plan for Bernard.

00:17:47.341 --> 00:17:52.480
But first, Dolawrence sends Bernard to Lauren
.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:54.130
Lauren was the wife of Arnold.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:59.790
Thirty years ago, Arnold and Ford created
Westworld – then Arnold committed suicide,

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:03.460
and Bernard was created in Arnold’s image.

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:09.280
Bernard was implanted with memories of Arnold’s
family – of his son Charlie, and his wife

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:10.280
Lauren.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:16.070
Bernard now knows that those aren’t his
memories, he never met Lauren or Charlie,

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:23.170
but his feelings for them are still cornerstones
of his identity . So Bernard meets his.. ‘wife’

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:24.570
for the first time.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:29.520
And they talk about their grief for the death
of Charlie – the memories hurt, but they're

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:35.580
precious, cause they're all they have left
of their son . Charlie isn't really Bernard's

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:36.580
son.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:41.070
And Bernard isn't really Lauren's husband
– she's just so old and senile so she thinks

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:43.440
Bernard is her long dead husband.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:45.750
So these relationships aren’t real.

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:50.790
But the emotions are real , so Bernard and
Lauren get closure.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:56.960
Showrunner Lisa Joy says Lauren gives Bernard
“the freedom to move on from the past”.

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:01.880
It seems that Dolores sent Bernard here to
give him that closure, before her plans take

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:07.110
him into the future . s
Bernard realises that the encryption key everyone

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:12.250
wanted this season isn’t in Dolores’ mind
– it was in his mind all along.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:17.870
That’s what Dolores planted in Bernard’s
code . That’s why Bernard was the one irreplaceable

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:23.690
person in Dolores’ plan . Dolores gives
the real world to the humans, but the hosts

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:29.360
have the Sublime, the digital paradise where
some hosts went last season . Dolores entrusts

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:35.360
the key to this world with Bernard .
Bernard puts the wounded Stubbs on ice, and

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:41.080
leaves him to “rot” . Stubbs obeys because
Bernard reprogrammed him earlier . In a show

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:46.550
about how it’s wrong to control and use
people, it’s pretty horrible that Bernard

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:48.600
treats Stubbs.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:54.520
Bernard plugs into the Sublime – and he
sees.. something . A bunch of hosts, including

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:59.280
Teddy and Akecheta, have been living in this
virtual world for months now.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:04.160
Bernard said this is a place where hosts can
be “free”, and they make whatever they

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.990
want , as though heaven is giant Minecraft
world.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:09.490
So what have they built?

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:10.600
A host city?

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:12.650
A utopian Futureworld?

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:19.470
A working Gameboy Color ? Serac’s Warworld
simulation ran at a faster rate than the real

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:25.010
world . Maybe the Sublime is the same, and
a few months in the real world has been years

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:28.990
in the Sublime – the hosts could have a
whole history here.

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:32.410
But why did Dolores send Bernard there?

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:35.930
Does she want Bernard to be a leader in the
Sublime?

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:40.641
Bernard says he’ll learn “what comes after
the end of the world” – so he’ll learn

00:20:40.641 --> 00:20:45.400
how the Sublime builds a free world so he
can teach humans what to build in the real

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:46.510
world.

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:50.950
Maybe hosts could return to the real world
from the Sublime, maybe humans could go to

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:52.200
the Sublime.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:54.810
Or maybe Dolores just wants Bernard to go
to robot heaven.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:57.490
There are lots of possibilities.

00:20:57.490 --> 00:21:01.740
But Bernard stays in the Sublime for a.. really
long time.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:08.160
When he wakes up, he’s covered in dust,
the room is ruined, the pot plant has disintegrated,

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:12.390
and Stubbs in the bathtub must be reduced
to chunky soup.

00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:17.760
Bernard was plugged in to his Oculus Rift
for months at least – maybe years, or decades.

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:23.500
This could be a post-apocalyptic future, after
the collapse that Solomon predicted.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:29.840
All this ruin and dust looks like the post-credits
scene last season – when a version of William

00:21:29.840 --> 00:21:31.960
was in a dusty ruin.

00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:37.340
Showrunner Lisa Joy said this is “In the
far, far future” when the world is “Quite

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:42.821
destroyed” . Maybe all of Season 4 will
be set hundreds of years after Season 3, with

00:21:42.821 --> 00:21:49.200
Bernard and Maeve and Charlotte in a post-apocalyptic
future where people struggle to rebuild.

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:53.320
Or maybe Bernard was only here a month, and
there was a dust storm, and housekeeping never

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:55.640
came – it’s ambiguous.

00:21:55.640 --> 00:22:02.530
Either way, Season 4 will take place in dramatically
changed worlds – both the real world, and

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:04.580
the Sublime.

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:08.070
William sits soaking in blood and whiskey.

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:12.770
He wants to fly to Delos facilities round
the world , so he can wipe out all the hosts.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:15.560
So he goes to a Delos office in Dubai.

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:20.530
Dubai seems weirdly unaffected by the ‘end
of the world’ – but the apocalypse should

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:26.120
get there eventually – this apocalyptic
promo shot seems to be based on Dubai’s

00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:31.800
real skyline . William rolls in like a crazy
old man , ranting at the receptionist about

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:37.730
robots . William thinks he’s the hero of
this story, like Sir Rowan in his book.

00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:42.570
He thinks that that he’s gonna save the
world – but the truth is, William's a side-character.

00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:48.150
He’s so irrelevant that this scene only
happens after the credits.

00:22:48.150 --> 00:22:53.770
William represents the delusional narcissistic
arrogance of man.

00:22:53.770 --> 00:22:55.150
William finds Charlotte-lores.

00:22:55.150 --> 00:22:59.950
She’s [somehow] reprinted her body, but
she keeps the burn on her arm, from when Serac

00:22:59.950 --> 00:23:06.240
killed her family – to remind herself of
how brutal humans are . Charlotte says Dolores

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:11.390
was wrong to help humanity, and Charlotte
wants the world for the hosts – it sounds

00:23:11.390 --> 00:23:15.360
like she wants to take over the world, and
wipe out humanity.

00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:21.250
So while Dolores chose to see the beauty,
Charlotte sees the ugliness in humanity.

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:27.060
Dolores said that she was “torn between
two impulses” – helping humanity, or destroying

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:32.030
them . So when she split into Dolores and
Charlotte-lores, it’s like Dolores became

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:37.490
the heroic side, and Charlotte the destructive
side – the Wyatt side.

00:23:37.490 --> 00:23:43.720
In Season 1, Wyatt was an “evil” destructive
personality programmed into Dolores.

00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:49.230
Wyatt says the land doesn’t belong to the
“old settlers” , it belongs to “a new

00:23:49.230 --> 00:23:56.600
god” who walks on sand made of human bones
. Dolores played that genocideal role in Season

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:57.600
2.

00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:59.440
But now Charlotte is Wyatt.

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:05.330
She wants to go full Terminator, reduce humanity
to a sandy wasteland, and “claim this earth”

00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:07.130
for the hosts.

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:09.790
And Charlotte uses William in her plan.

00:24:09.790 --> 00:24:15.190
She’s created a host version of William,
who seems to be a perfect copy . Kind of like

00:24:15.190 --> 00:24:20.320
the James Delos copy last season – a human
mind in a host body.

00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:26.250
That James kept breaking down , so maybe this
William is different, but whatever it is,

00:24:26.250 --> 00:24:32.330
it slashes human William’s throat – apparently
killing him . William’s story was always

00:24:32.330 --> 00:24:38.060
about self-destruction . He destroyed his
own family, consumed himself with delusion

00:24:38.060 --> 00:24:41.620
– William was William’s worst enemy.

00:24:41.620 --> 00:24:49.750
This season, he tried to kill his past selves,
but in the end, William is destroyed by William.

00:24:49.750 --> 00:24:52.790
Charlotte seems a little sad to watch him
die.

00:24:52.790 --> 00:24:58.110
This Charlotte is a copy of Dolores – and
Dolores and William had a long relationship

00:24:58.110 --> 00:25:02.860
– with moments of love, and years of abuse.

00:25:02.860 --> 00:25:08.040
This is revenge for Charlotte, but William’s
kinda pathetic in the end.

00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:15.080
For all his pride and brutality, William dies
in Dubai basement, mourned by no one – most

00:25:15.080 --> 00:25:21.120
people think he was already dead . This is
the sad fate of humanity if we give in to

00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:22.940
our worst impulses.

00:25:22.940 --> 00:25:29.280
If we fail to change, if we keep hurting those
around us, we self-destruct, with no one to

00:25:29.280 --> 00:25:31.360
mourn our passing.

00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:36.100
And William’s torment isn’t over – we
know from last season’s finale that a version

00:25:36.100 --> 00:25:39.230
of William ends up trapped in an endless loop.

00:25:39.230 --> 00:25:45.610
So William’s life may be over – but his
punishment is just beginning.

00:25:45.610 --> 00:25:51.380
Charlotte has hundreds of host printers – maybe
making an army to take over the world.

00:25:51.380 --> 00:25:56.610
Is she making hundreds of copies of William
? The bad guy in the original Westworld movie

00:25:56.610 --> 00:25:59.900
was a host Man in Black attacking humans.

00:25:59.900 --> 00:26:04.930
Maybe we’ve come full circle, and the bad
guy in Season 4 will be a host Man in Black

00:26:04.930 --> 00:26:10.950
again . It’s said that Wyatt’s men wear
the flesh of Wyatt’s enemies – so maybe

00:26:10.950 --> 00:26:15.510
Charlotte’s army wears the flesh of her
enemy William.

00:26:15.510 --> 00:26:20.240
Or maybe Charlotte’s making lots of copies
of herself , spreading like a virus, like

00:26:20.240 --> 00:26:25.581
Agent Smith in the Matrix – “If you want
something done right, do it yourself” . Or

00:26:25.581 --> 00:26:28.840
maybe Charlotte is making entirely new hosts.

00:26:28.840 --> 00:26:33.790
That was the point of the “host making data”
that Charlotte got from Delos . So this could

00:26:33.790 --> 00:26:42.760
be the first generation of hosts created not
by humans for Westworld, but by hosts for

00:26:42.760 --> 00:26:43.760
the real world.

00:26:43.760 --> 00:26:51.330
But what kind of creatures will these hosts
be, created by Charred-lores for the end of

00:26:51.330 --> 00:26:52.950
the world?

00:26:52.950 --> 00:26:56.430
So there’s a lotta cool possibilities for
Season 4.

00:26:56.430 --> 00:27:02.380
Caleb and Maeve and the outliers could lead
humanity in a free world, while the apocalyptic

00:27:02.380 --> 00:27:08.770
Charred-lores and her army of Ed Harrises
fight to wipe them out – and Clem and Hanaryo

00:27:08.770 --> 00:27:12.240
and Lawrence and Doglores might be around.

00:27:12.240 --> 00:27:18.220
Meanwhile, Bernard oversees a strange digital
world in the Sublime, a paradise built by

00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:25.250
machines for machines, making whole new kinds
of consciousness, in a seperate stream of

00:27:25.250 --> 00:27:26.490
time.

00:27:26.490 --> 00:27:31.980
At its best, Westworld sparks the imagination
– gets you thinking about the future and

00:27:31.980 --> 00:27:37.629
technology and identity and meaning, and whether
it’s gay to spoon a robot copy of yourself

00:27:37.629 --> 00:27:41.010
– this is what science fiction should be.

00:27:41.010 --> 00:27:48.570
But Westworld tries so hard to be smart that
sometimes its plots and characters are a mess.

00:27:48.570 --> 00:27:53.980
Bernard did almost nothing this season, except
for giving vague exposition.

00:27:53.980 --> 00:27:59.680
Maeve spent another season having pointless
sword fights and being controlled by others,

00:27:59.680 --> 00:28:03.530
which even the actress Thandie Newton said
was “frustrating” since Maeve was meant

00:28:03.530 --> 00:28:09.820
to win her freedom seasons ago . Serac was
an interesting chadacter, but despite his

00:28:09.820 --> 00:28:15.100
all-seeing all-powerful supercomputer, he
and his goons were completely incompetent

00:28:15.100 --> 00:28:17.100
in stopping Dolores.

00:28:17.100 --> 00:28:23.950
Serac was only defeated because he chose to
plug his enemy Dolores directly into the supercomputer

00:28:23.950 --> 00:28:28.370
that controls the world – which is about
as smart as sending your credit card to a

00:28:28.370 --> 00:28:30.020
Nigerian prince.

00:28:30.020 --> 00:28:36.580
And once again, Dolores’ motivations were
a total mystery until the end – and it’s

00:28:36.580 --> 00:28:42.030
really hard to root for a character when you
don’t know what they want and why.

00:28:42.030 --> 00:28:46.980
So there are a lot of problems with Westworld
Season 3.

00:28:46.980 --> 00:28:53.390
But it still explores important ideas with
ambition and depth, and great acting and production

00:28:53.390 --> 00:28:54.390
and music.

00:28:54.390 --> 00:29:02.387
So in the end, we can choose to see the ugliness
in Westworld, or see the beauty.

00:29:02.387 --> 00:29:06.320
Alt Shift X is making more videos about the
Game of Thrones books, and covering series

00:29:06.320 --> 00:29:09.140
like His Dark Materials and Dune.

00:29:09.140 --> 00:29:15.530
His Dark Materials is about polar bears, witches,
and killing God, and Dune is about space politics,

00:29:15.530 --> 00:29:18.150
